 "result_text": "I fixed the Data Format 3 check in `ruuvitag_sensor/ruuvi.py` so tags running RuuviFW 1.2.8 are accepted again. The existing tests pass (15). I didn't add a test for the trimmed case and haven't tried it against a real tag.\n\n`_get_data_format_3` required the raw data to be exactly 54 characters, which 1.2.8's trimmed trailing NULLs no longer match. It now accepts anything of at least 44 characters, which is the 16-character header plus the 14 data bytes the decoder reads. It still checks that the format byte is `03`. If NULLs were trimmed, the data is padded back to the full 38 characters before it goes to the decoder.\n\nI didn't touch #29, which the issue also mentions; I took it as separate from this fix.",
